            <ArticleTitle>Ehlers-Danlos syndrome associated with multiple spinal meningeal cysts--case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>380-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 40-year-old female with Ehlers-Danlos syndrome was admitted because of a large pelvic mass. Radiological examination revealed multiple spinal meningeal cysts. The first operation through a laminectomy revealed that the cysts originated from dilated dural sleeves containing nerve roots. Packing of dilated sleeves was inadequate. Finally the cysts were oversewed through a laparotomy. The cysts were reduced, but the postoperative course was complicated by poor wound healing and diffuse muscle atrophy. Ehlers-Danlos syndrome associated with spinal cysts may be best treated by endoscopic surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
